  "behavior": [
    "Token clones share the first scalar result while copied/restored token construction starts fresh state. Model finalization and sampled completion retain success or the exact first error, never pending false.",
    "Cached replay precedes native locking and still checks current producing-owner health; unrelated runtime contention cannot hide a remembered result.",
    "Production text completion queries only existing submitted event/model/sampling owners and creates no per-poll outer Scope. Short result/recovery loans end before callbacks and Drop; typed reentry/interruption does not prove completion.",
    "Closed all-strong Rc/Arc ownership retires the outer allocation before the cached payload/error. Existing source custody and model-state-preservation evidence remain unchanged."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "New token-state Rc and first-error Arc allocations and arbitrary escaping aliases require original pricing and finite population integration. Enclosing sizeof facts do not cover them.",
    "No original Scope contribution, role schedule, new hold/grant, later guard attachment or public managed route is introduced.",
    "Native Recovery/Scope/Record, source/root Vecs, nested graph and complete enclosing inventory remain separate obligations.",
    "Focused fresh-token construction tests supplement existing saved-copy/session/neutral driver coverage; no new released-checkpoint or native distributed run is claimed."
  ]
